# Path-versioned static assets.
#
# _VersionAsset($path, true) emits /SharedUI/css/tokens.<mtime>.css instead of
# /SharedUI/css/tokens.css?v=<mtime>. The query-string form is invisible to a CDN configured to
# ignore query strings — which is exactly why Core/UILibraries<YYYYMMDD>.js carries its version in
# the FILENAME. This rule gives CSS and JS the same lever without renaming anything on disk:
# the URL carries the mtime, the rewrite strips it, Apache serves the real file.
#
# The mtime is a 9-or-more digit unix timestamp, which is what keeps this from colliding with a
# genuine file like `jquery.min.js` or `foo.2.css`.
#
# Game storage is never served. <Root>/Games/<id>/ holds the full gamestate (both players' hands and decks,
# undo snapshots, sideboard/rematch pointers) plus the GameIDCounter — all of it read by PHP from disk,
# none of it meant for a browser. Until 2026-10-08 any of it was one GET away. 404, not 403, so a probe
# cannot even confirm that a game id exists.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On
  RewriteRule (^|/)Games(/|$) - [R=404,NC,L]
  RewriteRule ^(.+)\.[0-9]{9,}\.(css|js)$ $1.$2 [L]
</IfModule>
